# Home Assistant MQTT + Automations debug with httpyac
#
# How to use:
# 1) Create documents/httpyac.env.json from the provided sample and set baseUrl/token
# 2) In VS Code, click "Send Request" above a block to execute it
# 3) For WebSocket, run the WS block; you should see live state_changed events
#
# Notes:
# - nest/setpoint_cool/cmd is non-retained. Have listeners open before publishing if you want to see it in HA's MQTT Listen tool.
# - All "state" topics are expected to be retained so the TFT seeds on connect.

### Test HA connectivity
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Reload automations after YAML changes
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/services/automation/reload
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Publish TFT-style setpoint command (°C, non-retained)
# COOL mode => HA should call climate.set_temperature with temperature (rounded to whole °F)
# HEATCOOL => HA should call climate.set_temperature with target_temp_high
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/services/mqtt/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "topic": "nest/setpoint_cool/cmd",
  "payload": "23.0",
  "retain": false,
  "qos": 1
}

### Clear stale retained command (one-time if needed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/services/mqtt/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "topic": "nest/setpoint_cool/cmd",
  "payload": "",
  "retain": true
}

### Manually seed TFT state: ambient °C (retained)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/services/mqtt/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "topic": "nest/ambient/state",
  "payload": "24.0",
  "retain": true
}

### Manually seed TFT state: humidity % (retained)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/services/mqtt/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "topic": "nest/humidity/state",
  "payload": "64",
  "retain": true
}

### Manually seed TFT state: setpoint °C (retained)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/services/mqtt/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "topic": "nest/setpoint_cool/state",
  "payload": "22.0",
  "retain": true
}

### Inspect climate state (check hvac_mode, temperature fields)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/states/climate.living_room
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### WebSocket: watch live state_changed events
# In the response tab, after auth, you should see stream of events. Move TFT dial or change Nest to observe updates.
WS ws://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/websocket

{"type":"auth","access_token":"{{token}}"}
{"id": 1, "type": "subscribe_events", "event_type": "state_changed"}
